-- ccc32-nif-soirsa.l4 -- AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE: 2026, c. 16, ss 48 to 52, replacing parts of sections 490.02, 490.022, 490.04, 490.05 and 490.06 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46
-- (exemption orders and terminations of the duty to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, adding the National Defence Act and the International Transfer of Offenders Act routes;
-- lines 19692-19744 of the text). Section 53 (a wording change in Form 52) is machinery (reason 2) and has no function.
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. This is a SECOND, FUTURE text of provisions that ccc18 encodes in their in-force form: every name here carries `(not in force)` after the section label so that it cannot collide with theirs.
-- NOTHING in this module says the text is law today. WHERE THE TEXT GIVES ONLY THE REPLACED PARAGRAPH (the lead-in of 490.04(1) and 490.05(1), and the paragraphs of 490.04(3), 490.05(3) and 490.05(5) around the replaced one are in-force text of ccc18),
-- an item outside the replaced paragraph is NOT COVERED (points outside the text); this module does not reconstruct the surrounding section.
-- How a result reads, the naming rule and the rule for days the text leaves open: see the head of ccc32-related-1.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `2026, c. 16, ss. 48 and 49 -- references read as of a day (subsections 490.02(3) and 490.022(4))`

-- 48 Subsection 490.02(3) is replaced by: (3) The reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before October 26, 2023,
-- the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3) is a reference to that provision as it read from time to time before that day and the reference in that paragraph to subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act
-- is a reference to that provision as it read from time to time before the day on which section 48 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force.
-- A rule of reading over a small typed representation of the reference: the answer is the day BEFORE which the provision is read.
-- src:19694 | References
-- src:19695 | (3) The reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before October 26, 2023, the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3) is a reference to that provision as it read from time to time before that day and the reference in that paragraph to subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act is a reference to that provision as it read from time to time before the day on which section 48 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force.
@ref s 490.02(3) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 48 (src:19694-19695)
DECLARE `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence`
    `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3)`
    `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act`
    `s 490.02(3) (not in force) another reference`

@ref s 490.02(3) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 48 (src:19694-19695)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference`
      `the day on which section 48 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.02(3) (not in force) the day before which the provision referred to is read` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence` THEN JUST (Date 26 10 2023)
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3)` THEN JUST (Date 26 10 2023)
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) (not in force) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act` THEN JUST `the day on which section 48 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force`
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) (not in force) another reference` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before October 26, 2023"

-- 49 Subsection 490.022(4) is replaced by: (4) In paragraph (3)(d), the reference to the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before October 26, 2023
-- and the reference to the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before the day on which section 49 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force.
-- src:19699 | References
-- src:19700 | (4) In paragraph (3)(d), the reference to the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before October 26, 2023 and the reference to the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before the day on which section 49 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force.
@ref s 490.022(4) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 49 (src:19699-19700)
DECLARE `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference to the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code`
    `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference to the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act`
    `s 490.022(4) (not in force) another reference`

@ref s 490.022(4) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 49 (src:19699-19700)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference`
      `the day on which section 49 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.022(4) (not in force) the day before which the definition referred to is read` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference to the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code` THEN JUST (Date 26 10 2023)
    WHEN `s 490.022(4) (not in force) the reference to the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act` THEN JUST `the day on which section 49 of the Military Justice System Modernization Act comes into force`
    WHEN `s 490.022(4) (not in force) another reference` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In paragraph (3)(d), the reference to the definition designated offence"

§ `2026, c. 16, s. 50 -- section 490.04 (application for an exemption order from an order to comply)`

-- 50 (1) Paragraphs 490.04(1)(a) and (b) are replaced by: (a) an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before October 26, 2023; (a.1) an order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act on or after April 15, 2011
-- but before the day on which this paragraph comes into force; or (b) an obligation under section 490.02901, or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, that began before October 26, 2023.
-- (a) and (a.1) fix a window of dates in the text's own words: outside it the text says no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); (b) fixes only "before": outside it NOT COVERED (ruling (c)).
-- src:19704 | (a) an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before October 26, 2023;
-- src:19705 | (a.1) an order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act on or after April 15, 2011 but before the day on which this paragraph comes into force; or
-- src:19706 | (b) an obligation under section 490.02901, or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, that began before October 26, 2023.
@ref s 490.04(1)(a), (a.1) and (b) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 50(1) (src:19704-19706)
DECLARE `s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.04(1)(a) (not in force) an order made under section 490.012`
    `s 490.04(1)(a.1) (not in force) an order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act`
    `s 490.04(1)(b) (not in force) an obligation under section 490.02901`
    `s 490.04(1)(b) (not in force) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    `s 490.04(1) (not in force) something else`

@ref s 490.04(1)(a), (a.1) and (b) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 50(1) (src:19704-19706)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation`
      `the day the order was made or the obligation began` IS A DATE
      `the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a.1) comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation is one listed in paragraph (a), (a.1) or (b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 490.04(1)(a) (not in force) an order made under section 490.012` THEN
        IF `the day the order was made or the obligation began` AT LEAST (Date 15 4 2011) AND `the day the order was made or the obligation began` LESS THAN (Date 26 10 2023)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before October 26, 2023"
    WHEN `s 490.04(1)(a.1) (not in force) an order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act` THEN
        IF `the day the order was made or the obligation began` AT LEAST (Date 15 4 2011) AND `the day the order was made or the obligation began` LESS THAN `the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a.1) comes into force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act on or after April 15, 2011 but before the day on which this paragraph comes into force"
    WHEN `s 490.04(1)(b) (not in force) an obligation under section 490.02901` THEN
        IF `the day the order was made or the obligation began` LESS THAN (Date 26 10 2023)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that began before October 26, 2023"
    WHEN `s 490.04(1)(b) (not in force) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` THEN
        IF `the day the order was made or the obligation began` LESS THAN (Date 26 10 2023)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that began before October 26, 2023"
    WHEN `s 490.04(1) (not in force) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the lead-in of subsection 490.04(1) is in-force text of part ccc18

-- (2) [as replaced] A person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b) if, on or after October 26, 2023, they have made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation.
