      `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.23(2) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(3)(a) (not in force) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction is a court that may receive the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
       OR (`the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1) or (b.1)` AND `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.23(2) of the National Defence Act`)
