§ `2026, c. 16, s. 52 -- subsection 490.06(2) (appeal court: removal of information from the database)`

-- 52 Subsection 490.06(2) is replaced by: (2) If an appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person
-- that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be.
-- src:19743 | Removal of information from database
-- src:19744 | (2) If an appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be.
@ref s 490.06(2) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 52 (src:19743-19744)
DECLARE `s 490.06(2) (not in force) what the information was registered on receipt of` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) a copy of the order made under section 490.012`
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) a copy of the order made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act`
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) the notice referred to in section 490.02901`
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) something else`

@ref s 490.06(2) as replaced by 2026, c. 16, s. 52 (src:19743-19744)
GIVEN `the appeal court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
      source IS A `s 490.06(2) (not in force) what the information was registered on receipt of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.06(2) (not in force) the appeal court shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information from the database` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information"
        IF source EQUALS `s 490.06(2) (not in force) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of the order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
